9-mid-air-brawl/articleshow/134642914.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T21:24:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajesh Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134643072,imgsize-1434501.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Akhilesh Yadav's Rajya Sabha picks: Samajwadi Party's master strategy or 'PDA' contradiction?]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akhilesh-yadavs-rajya-sabha-picks-samajwadi-partys-master-strategy-or-pda-contradiction/articleshow/134642605.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134642605.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Samajwadi Party chief Akhilesh Yadav's Rajya Sabha picks, including uncle Ram Gopal Yadav and Reliance executive Dhanraj Parimal Nathwani, are being seen as an early test for the 2027 Uttar Pradesh assembly polls. The nominations raise questions over the SP's PDA strategy, its broader political outreach and a possible third Rajya Sabha candidate, despite the party's numbers falling short of the winning quota.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akhilesh-yadavs-rajya-sabha-picks-samajwadi-partys-master-strategy-or-pda-contradiction/articleshow/134642605.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akhilesh-yadavs-rajya-sabha-picks-samajwadi-partys-master-strategy-or-pda-contradiction/articleshow/134642605.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T20:57:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pallavi</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134642772,imgsize-1412273.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Warring out, Channi not in: Has Congress solved Punjab crisis or created more confusion?]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/warring-out-channi-not-in-yet-has-congress-solved-punjab-crisis-or-created-more-confusion/articleshow/134640757.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134640757.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Amarinder Singh Raja Warring has resigned as the president of the Punjab Congress after more than four years. His resignation follows a prolonged period of infighting over leadership roles within the party. Both Charanjit Singh Channi and Warring have seen shifts in their status amid ongoing power struggles.  But has Congress really solved the Punjab crisis?]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/warring-out-channi-not-in-yet-has-congress-solved-punjab-crisis-or-created-more-confusion/articleshow/134640757.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/warring-out-channi-not-in-yet-has-congress-solved-punjab-crisis-or-created-more-confusion/articleshow/134640757.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T20:07:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Mukherjee</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134641964,imgsize-811202.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Their time is up': Akhilesh Yadav slams Centre over police action at Jantar Mantar protest against CEC]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/their-time-is-up-akhilesh-yadav-slams-centre-over-police-action-at-jantar-mantar-protest-against-cec/articleshow/134641426.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134641426.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/their-time-is-up-akhilesh-yadav-slams-centre-over-police-action-at-jantar-mantar-protest-against-cec/articleshow/134641426.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/their-time-is-up-akhilesh-yadav-slams-centre-over-police-action-at-jantar-mantar-protest-against-cec/articleshow/134641426.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T19:36:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134641558,imgsize-74578.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[From papads to pitches: NCERT brings startup lessons to Class IX]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/from-papads-to-pitches-ncert-brings-startup-lessons-to-class-ix/articleshow/134640986.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134640986.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A new chapter on startups and entrepreneurship has been introduced for Class IX students in NCERT textbooks. The chapter emphasizes the growth of India's startup ecosystem over the past decade. It includes important lessons on identifying business opportunities and creating effective business plans. Entrepreneurial stories, including those of Lijjat Papad and Mohan Singh Oberoi, illustrate key concepts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/from-papads-to-pitches-ncert-brings-startup-lessons-to-class-ix/articleshow/134640986.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/from-papads-to-pitches-ncert-brings-startup-lessons-to-class-ix/articleshow/134640986.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T19:00:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Manash Pratim Gohain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134641010,imgsize-56806.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Evening news wrap: India women’s hockey team wins Asian Games gold; CJP's Abhijeet Dipke launches ‘Jail Bharo Andolan’ &amp; more]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-india-womens-hockey-team-wins-asian-games-gold-cjps-abhijeet-dipke-launches-jail-bharo-andolan-more/articleshow/134640611.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134640611.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India’s women’s hockey team secured the Asian Games gold medal by defeating China 1-0 in the final. Abhijeet Dipke initiated a "Jail Bharo Andolan" in Mumbai over alleged electoral issues, calling for the election chief's resignation. A Flydubai mid-air incident was termed a 'terrorist act,' with praise for the Indian pilot's actions. Amarinder Singh Raja Warring resigned as Punjab Congress chief after years of leadership amid factional dissent.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-india-womens-hockey-team-wins-asian-games-gold-cjps-abhijeet-dipke-launches-jail-bharo-andolan-more/articleshow/134640611.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-india-womens-hockey-team-wins-asian-games-gold-cjps-abhijeet-dipke-launches-jail-bharo-andolan-more/articleshow/134640611.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T18:52:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134640901,imgsize-1665817.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['May Bapu’s timeless message keep guiding us': PM Modi pays tribute to Mahatma Gandhi, attends prayer meet]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/may-bapus-timeless-message-keep-guiding-us-pm-modi-pays-tribute-to-mahatma-gandhi-attends-prayer-meet/articleshow/134639962.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134639962.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Prime Minister Narendra Modi participated in a special interfaith prayer meeting to honor Mahatma Gandhi's birth anniversary. He paid floral tributes at Gandhi Smriti and Rajghat earlier in the day. PM Modi emphasized Gandhi's ideals of truth, peace, and non-violence while urging people to adopt Swadeshi. Vice President CP Radhakrishnan also attended and remembered Gandhi's contributions to India's freedom movement.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/may-bapus-timeless-message-keep-guiding-us-pm-modi-pays-tribute-to-mahatma-gandhi-attends-prayer-meet/articleshow/134639962.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/may-bapus-timeless-message-keep-guiding-us-pm-modi-pays-tribute-to-mahatma-gandhi-attends-prayer-meet/articleshow/134639962.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T18:23:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134640194,imgsize-83744.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[2 Jharkhand yoga instructors killed in Vietnam road accident; bodies to be brought back on Oct 3]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/2-jharkhand-yoga-instructors-killed-in-vietnam-road-accident-bodies-to-be-brought-back-on-oct-3/articleshow/134640059.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134640059.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Tragedy struck as two beloved yoga instructors, Raja Kumar and Vinay Kumar Rai, lost their lives in a tragic road accident in Vietnam. The financial burden of repatriating their remains prompted an outpouring of support from the local community. In a gesture of assistance, the Jharkhand government pledged Rs 5 lakh for each family.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/2-jharkhand-yoga-instructors-killed-in-vietnam-road-accident-bodies-to-be-brought-back-on-oct-3/articleshow/134640059.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/2-jharkhand-yoga-instructors-killed-in-vietnam-road-accident-bodies-to-be-brought-back-on-oct-3/articleshow/134640059.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T18:17:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134640120,imgsize-94251.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Watch: Tamil Nadu CM Vijay’s ‘chai pe charcha’ during bypoll campaign trail]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-tamil-nadu-cm-vijays-chai-pe-charcha-during-bypoll-campaign-trail/articleshow/134639419.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134639419.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-tamil-nadu-cm-vijays-chai-pe-charcha-during-bypoll-campaign-trail/articleshow/134639419.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-tamil-nadu-cm-vijays-chai-pe-charcha-during-bypoll-campaign-trail/articleshow/134639419.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T17:58:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134640212,imgsize-6995043.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Gandhi Jayanti: Mamata says stronger India must be guided by Bapu’s ideals]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gandhi-jayanti-mamata-says-stronger-india-must-be-guided-by-bapus-ideals/articleshow/134638680.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134638680.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[On Gandhi Jayanti, Mamata Banerjee paid tribute to Mahatma Gandhi, underscoring his timeless principles for strengthening India. She emphasized that his messages of truth, simplicity, and service are essential for national advancement. Additionally, Abhishek Banerjee honored Gandhi’s unwavering dedication to truth, justice, and equality. Together, they urged for an inclusive nation where respect for citizens' rights and dignity is upheld, underpinned by the guiding principles of the Constitution.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gandhi-jayanti-mamata-says-stronger-india-must-be-guided-by-bapus-ideals/articleshow/134638680.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gandhi-jayanti-mamata-says-stronger-india-must-be-guided-by-bapus-ideals/articleshow/134638680.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T17:42:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134638806,imgsize-150425.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Exceptional courage': Pilots body writes to PM Modi, requests bravery award for Smit Machchhar]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/exceptional-courage-pilots-body-writes-to-pm-modi-requests-bravery-award-for-smit-machchhar/articleshow/134638509.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134638509.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/exceptional-courage-pilots-body-writes-to-pm-modi-requests-bravery-award-for-smit-machchhar/articleshow/134638509.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/exceptional-courage-pilots-body-writes-to-pm-modi-requests-bravery-award-for-smit-machchhar/articleshow/134638509.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T17:13:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org