k><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/raja-ki-chutti-karni-chahiye-amarinder-warring-submits-resignation-after-meeting-rahul-gandhi-blames-sachin-pilot/articleshow/134636599.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T15:36:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134636607,imgsize-61192.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India’s great hunt for oil: Inside the ₹84,000-crore Samudra Manthan mission]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indias-great-hunt-for-oil-inside-the-84000-crore-samudra-manthan-mission/articleshow/134636556.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134636556.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India is pushing for increased exploration of offshore oil and gas resources in various basins. The government has initiated the Samudra Manthan scheme to support these exploration efforts financially and structurally. Key basins include Mahanadi, Andaman-Nicobar, Krishna-Godavari, and Cauvery, each with significant potential. Officials emphasize the importance of infrastructure to develop discoveries efficiently and cost-effectively.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indias-great-hunt-for-oil-inside-the-84000-crore-samudra-manthan-mission/articleshow/134636556.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indias-great-hunt-for-oil-inside-the-84000-crore-samudra-manthan-mission/articleshow/134636556.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T15:34:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134636603,imgsize-120867.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Women farmers need greater role in agricultural policymaking: RSS leader Ramlal]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/women-farmers-need-greater-role-in-agricultural-policymaking-rss-leader-ramlal/articleshow/134636372.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134636372.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[At a recent conference, RSS leader Ramlal highlighted the growing importance of women farmers in Indian agriculture. With around 5,000 participants in Delhi advocating for reforms, topics like organic farming and fair pricing took center stage. Ramlal called for policy adjustments that prioritize women farmers’ contributions, emphasizing their role in shaping the future of agriculture and traditional farming methods.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/women-farmers-need-greater-role-in-agricultural-policymaking-rss-leader-ramlal/articleshow/134636372.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/women-farmers-need-greater-role-in-agricultural-policymaking-rss-leader-ramlal/articleshow/134636372.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T15:30:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134636416,imgsize-49852.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘They are all chasing the CM’s chair’: Punjab BJP chief Kewal Dhillon accuses Congress of infighting after Warring’s resignation]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/i-dont-have-concrete-proof-warring-hints-at-pilots-role-in-punjab-congress-leadership-change-ahead-of-2027-polls/articleshow/134636454.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134636454.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Amarinder Singh Raja Warring has suggested his removal from the Punjab Congress chief post is imminent. Internal divisions have prompted calls for leadership change ahead of the 2027 assembly elections. Warring expressed satisfaction with his tenure, despite challenges and differences within the party. Several candidates are being considered to replace him in the upcoming announcement. The party high command will make the final decision on the new leadership.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/i-dont-have-concrete-proof-warring-hints-at-pilots-role-in-punjab-congress-leadership-change-ahead-of-2027-polls/articleshow/134636454.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/i-dont-have-concrete-proof-warring-hints-at-pilots-role-in-punjab-congress-leadership-change-ahead-of-2027-polls/articleshow/134636454.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T15:28:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134639489,imgsize-928063.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Uttarakhand CM Pushkar Dhami pays tribute to Mahatma Gandhi, Lal Bahadur Shastri on birth anniversary]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/uttarakhand-cm-pushkar-dhami-pays-tribute-to-mahatma-gandhi-lal-bahadur-shastri-on-birth-anniversary/articleshow/134636518.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134636518.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Uttarakhand Chief Minister Pushkar Singh Dhami paid floral tributes and paid homage to Mahatma Gandhi and former Prime Minister and Bharat Ratna Lal Bahadur Shastri at the Chief Minister's residence on Friday on the occasion of their birth anniversaries.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/uttarakhand-cm-pushkar-dhami-pays-tribute-to-mahatma-gandhi-lal-bahadur-shastri-on-birth-anniversary/articleshow/1346